abstract: >-
  Technical reproduction package for a fixed-checkpoint study of local event
  geometry in SpikeSCR on Spiking Speech Commands. The experiment evaluates
  725,070 neighboring inputs from 100 validation utterances, measures activation
  changes at seven network boundaries, and records 180,740 activation-replacement
  score vectors. The package includes the frozen checkpoint, transformed inputs,
  recorded outputs, statistical regeneration, and model-replay tools with
  numerical conformance checks. Later records add finite margin/gradient search
  comparisons, paired count-readout replicas, full-validation padding and q/k
  isolation controls, and paired CPU/GPU replay of 25,820 class-changing
  candidates. The associated manuscript is Aggregate accuracy conceals
  concentrated temporal vulnerability in a spiking speech classifier.
  Validation coverage and replay limitations are
  documented in the repository. Original project software is licensed under MIT;
  project-authored research outputs, documentation and model weights are licensed
  under CC BY 4.0, within the author's rights. Dataset attribution and third-party
  software terms remain in force; see LICENSE_NOTICE.md for the file-level scope.
keywords:
